You are debugging a production issue where an order processing workflow fails to persist fallback records. When downstream payment fails, the service catches the exception and attempts to update the order status to `FAILED_PAYMENT` in the database, but the client receives an unexpected `500 Internal Server Error` and the database transaction is completely aborted.

java
@Service
public class OrderWorkflowService {
    @Autowired
    private PaymentProcessingService paymentProcessingService;
    @Autowired
    private OrderRepository orderRepository;

    @Transactional
    public void processOrder(Order order) {
        try {
            paymentProcessingService.executePayment(order);
        } catch (PaymentFailedException ex) {
            order.setStatus(OrderStatus.PAYMENT_RETRY_PENDING);
            orderRepository.save(order);
        }
    }
}

@Service
public class PaymentProcessingService {
    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRED)
    public void executePayment(Order order) {
        if (!externalPaymentGateway.charge(order)) {
            throw new PaymentFailedException("Declined by payment processor"); // Extends RuntimeException
        }
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an API gateway orchestrates distributed microservice calls using a scatter-gather pattern. During peak hours, an intermittent downstream network outage causes connection timeouts. Shortly thereafter, the entire JVM becomes completely unresponsive: all health checks fail, pending asynchronous requests stall indefinitely, and thread dumps reveal dozens of worker threads stuck in `WAITING`.

